WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.112
A mature detection lifecycle program defines how detections are requested, prioritized,

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:08.757
designed, documented, tested, deployed, tuned, reviewed, and retired.

00:00:08.757 --> 00:00:13.768
It assigns ownership and encourages collaboration among detection engineers, SOC analysts,

00:00:13.768 --> 00:00:16.958
threat hunters, incident responders, and security leaders.

00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:20.602
The goal is not simply having many detections.

00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:27.437
The goal is maintaining a reliable portfolio of signals that helps defenders make better decisions.

00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:31.537
A strong program connects telemetry, threat knowledge, analyst feedback,

00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:32.904
and changing environments.

00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:37.460
It uses continuous improvement to keep detections useful over time.
